@startuml
title Cache Sequence Diagrams\nRedis (Primary) + CSC (Local) + Caffeine (Fallback)

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 200

participant "Service" as Svc #E8EAF6
participant "Circuit\nBreaker" as CB #FFF9C4
participant "Redis CSC\n(JVM-local)" as CSC #E3F2FD
participant "Redis\nServer" as Redis #FFF3E0
participant "Caffeine\n(In-Memory)" as Caff #E8F5E9
database "Database" as DB #F3E5F5

== **Scenario 1: Cache Populate (Cold Start / Cache Miss)** ==

Svc -> CB : get(key)
activate CB
CB -> CSC : GET(key)
activate CSC
CSC -> CSC : lookup local cache
CSC --> CB : **CSC MISS**
deactivate CSC

CB -> Redis : GET(key) [network call]
activate Redis
Redis --> CB : **Redis MISS**
deactivate Redis

CB -> DB : query(key)
activate DB
DB --> CB : data
deactivate DB

CB -> Redis : SET(key, data, TTL)
activate Redis
Redis --> CB : OK
deactivate Redis

note over CSC : CSC auto-populated\nvia CLIENT TRACKING\non SET/GET response

CB -> Caff : put(key, data)
activate Caff
Caff --> CB : OK
deactivate Caff

CB --> Svc : data
deactivate CB

note over Svc
    **Result:** Key now cached in:
    • Redis Server (primary)
    • Redis CSC (JVM-local, auto)
    • Caffeine (in-memory fallback)
end note

== **Scenario 2: Cache Hit (CSC Hit — Zero Network)** ==

Svc -> CB : get(key)
activate CB
CB -> CSC : GET(key)
activate CSC
CSC -> CSC : lookup local cache
CSC --> CB : **CSC HIT** ✓\nreturn data locally
deactivate CSC

note over CSC : No network call to Redis.\nServed entirely from JVM.

CB --> Svc : data
deactivate CB

note over Svc
    **Result:** Returned from CSC
    • **0 network calls**
    • Fastest path after cold start
end note

== **Scenario 3: Redis Down — Caffeine Miss → DB Fallback** ==

Svc -> CB : get(key)
activate CB

CB -> CSC : GET(key)
activate CSC
CSC -> Redis : GET(key) [network call]
activate Redis
Redis --> CSC !! : **Connection Failed**\nJedisConnectionException
deactivate Redis
CSC --> CB : **FAILURE**
deactivate CSC

note over CB #FFF176 : Circuit Breaker **OPENS**\nRedis marked unavailable

CB -> Caff : get(key)
activate Caff
Caff -> Caff : lookup heap cache
Caff --> CB : **Caffeine MISS**
deactivate Caff

CB -> DB : query(key)
activate DB
DB --> CB : data
deactivate DB

CB -> Caff : put(key, data)
activate Caff
Caff --> CB : OK
deactivate Caff

CB --> Svc : data
deactivate CB

note over Svc
    **Result:** Served from DB
    • Caffeine populated for next call
    • Redis skipped (circuit open)
    • Degraded mode active
end note

== **Scenario 4: Redis Down — Caffeine Hit (Degraded Mode)** ==

Svc -> CB : get(key)
activate CB

note over CB #FFF176 : Circuit still **OPEN**\nSkip Redis entirely

CB -> Caff : get(key)
activate Caff
Caff -> Caff : lookup heap cache
Caff --> CB : **Caffeine HIT** ✓\nreturn cached data
deactivate Caff

CB --> Svc : data (possibly stale)
deactivate CB

note over Svc
    **Result:** Served from Caffeine
    • **0 network calls**
    • Data may be stale
    • App remains responsive
    • Circuit will probe Redis
      periodically (HALF_OPEN)
end note

== **Scenario 5: Redis Comes Back Online — Clear Caffeine** ==

note over CB #C8E6C9 : Circuit transitions to **HALF_OPEN**\nProbe Redis with test call

Svc -> CB : get(key) [or scheduled probe]
activate CB

CB -> CSC : GET(key)
activate CSC
CSC -> Redis : GET(key) [probe]
activate Redis
Redis --> CSC : **SUCCESS** ✓\nRedis is back
deactivate Redis
CSC --> CB : data
deactivate CSC

note over CB #C8E6C9 : Circuit transitions to **CLOSED**\nRedis marked available

CB -> Caff : **clear()** ☐\nevict ALL entries
activate Caff
note over Caff #FFCDD2
    Caffeine data may be **stale**
    (written during Redis outage
    or missed invalidation events).
    Full clear ensures consistency
    with Redis as source of truth.
end note
Caff --> CB : cleared
deactivate Caff

CB --> Svc : data (fresh from Redis)
deactivate CB

note over Svc
    **Result:** Redis recovered
    • Circuit **CLOSED** — normal flow resumes
    • Caffeine **cleared** — no stale data
    • CSC re-populates automatically
    • Subsequent reads follow Scenario 1 or 2
end note

@enduml
